    Recommend tenant-specific admin role in multi-tenancy guide (#8283)
    
    The multi-tenancy guide's example tenant configuration used
    admin_role=ROLE_ADMIN. ROLE_ADMIN is Opencast's global administrator
    role and grants administrative access across all tenants, so reusing it
    for an individual tenant gives that tenant's administrators privileges
    far beyond their own tenant.
    
    Use a tenant-specific administrator role (e.g. ROLE_TENANT1_ADMIN) in
    the example instead, explain why, and describe how to grant that role
    access in the tenant's security configuration. The default organization
    keeps ROLE_ADMIN, since its administrator is the system-wide one.
    
